From 0cca844a5decea46a9276d3ad8f2eebc64dac82c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A'rpi <arpi.git@interoot.hu>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:07:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add a built-in sftp server, like OpenSSH internal-sftp

With DROPBEAR_SFTP_INTERNAL a command of exactly "internal-sftp", from
SFTPSERVER_PATH, a forced command or an sftp chroot, is served by the
new src/svr-sftp.c in the session child instead of exec()ing a
program. No binary, libraries or device nodes are needed, so it works
inside a chroot and on systems without OpenSSH's sftp-server.

It implements SFTP protocol version 3 (draft-ietf-secsh-filexfer-02)
with the OpenSSH extensions posix-rename, statvfs, fstatvfs, hardlink,
fsync and limits, which is what the OpenSSH sftp client uses. realpath
tolerates a missing last component like OpenSSH, the client depends on
that for "put -r". Packets are parsed with bounds checks and a
malformed packet ends the session. Logging only goes to syslog, with
LOG_COMMANDS every modifying operation is logged.

The protocol code only uses libc and can be built standalone for
testing with the OpenSSH client:

    cc -DSFTP_STANDALONE -o sftp-test src/svr-sftp.c
    sftp -D ./sftp-test

Disabled by default with DROPBEAR_SFTP_INTERNAL 0.
